 "notes": "Chart 15 (pages 130-131). Left page (p.130) carries only the two printed annotations plus page number; ledger grid is entirely on the right page (p.131). Four carried-forward pivotal-point rows sit above the DATE header row (UT, then NRC, then NR, then NRC again on the same line as the printed \"1939\" year label) before the dated grid begins at NOV.24. All rows from DEC.15 through JAN.6 (SAT.16, 18-22, SAT.23, 26-29, SAT.30, JAN.2-5, SAT.6) are blank/unused except the DEC.14 entries noted above. A new year \"1940\" (written smaller, above \"JAN.2\") appears printed in the date column directly below \"SAT.30\", marking the year rollover mid-chart; no further handwritten entries follow it on this spread. All checksums (KP = US + BS) verified consistent for every row where multiple instruments have entries, using carry-forward of the last recorded value when one instrument is blank on a given date (SAT.25 and DEC.14 rows).",
